window.__CAPM_DATA=(window.__CAPM_DATA||"")+"\\\"/><\\/div><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\">A. Construction work requires a building permit from the City council: EEF<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">B. Workers who don’t obey safety rules will be penalized: OPA<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">C.<span> <\\/span>Only authorized personnel are allowed on site: OPA<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">D. Workers have expertise in infrastructure construction: EEF<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer: A. Construction work requires a building permit from the City council: EEF B. Workers who don’t obey safety rules will be penalized: OPA C. Only authorized personnel are allowed on site: OPA D. Workers have expertise in infrastructure construction: EEF\",\"type\":\"mapping\",\"special\":{\"type\":\"mapping\",\"targets\":[[\"A\",\"A. Construction work requires a building permit from the City council\"],[\"B\",\"B. Workers who don’t obey safety rules will be penalized\"],[\"C\",\"C. Only authorized personnel are allowed on site\"],[\"D\",\"D. Workers have expertise in infrastructure construction\"]],\"options\":[[\"eef\",\"Enterprise Environmental Factors (EEFs)\"],[\"opa\",\"Organizational Process Assets (OPAs)\"]],\"correct\":{\"A\":\"eef\",\"B\":\"opa\",\"C\":\"opa\",\"D\":\"eef\"},\"note\":\"The EPUB includes answer-labelled text directly after the question image. Exam mode hides those spoiler lines and uses the source image/items as the interactive prompt; the original answer material is preserved in review.\"},\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"The EPUB includes answer-labelled text directly after the question image. Exam mode hides those spoiler lines and uses the source image/items as the interactive prompt; the original answer material is preserved in review.\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":64,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">An Entity-Relationship Diagram (ERD) is a model that illustrates the business data requirements, including the various pieces of information and their interrelationships. What type of model does the ERD represent?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An Entity-Relationship Diagram (ERD) is a model that illustrates the business data requirements, including the various pieces of information and their interrelationships. What type of model does the ERD represent?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scope model<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Scope model\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Process model<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Process model\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Rule model<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Rule model\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Data model<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Data model\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Interface model<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Interface model\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Data models are structured representations that document how data is stored, organized, and flows within a system. They include entity relationship diagrams, data flow diagrams, and data dictionaries<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Scope models are frameworks that systematically structure and organize the features, functions, and boundaries of the business domain under analysis. They include context diagrams, use case diagrams, and SWOT.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Process models represent and document business processes and system features. They include process flow, user story and use case.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Rule models outline business constraints, rules, and mandatory procedures that establish the definitive criteria for validating any proposed solution. They include the decision tree, decision table, and business rules catalog.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option E:<\\/span> Interface models clarify how systems interact and relate to one another within a solution. They include user interface flow, wireframes, and display action response.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Data models are structured representations that document how data is stored, organized, and flows within a system. They include entity relationship diagrams, data flow diagrams, and data dictionaries . Option A: Scope models are frameworks that systematically structure and organize the features, functions, and boundaries of the business domain under analysis. They include context diagrams, use case diagrams, and SWOT. Option B: Process models represent and document business processes and system features. They include process flow, user story and use case. Option C: Rule models outline business constraints, rules, and mandatory procedures that establish the definitive criteria for validating any proposed solution. They include the decision tree, decision table, and business rules catalog. Option E: Interface models clarify how systems interact and relate to one another within a solution. They include user interface flow, wireframes, and display action response.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":65,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In business analysis, which of the following statements accurately reflects the relationship between project life cycles and product life cycles?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In business analysis, which of the following statements accurately reflects the relationship between project life cycles and product life cycles?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A project life cycle consists of multiple product life cycles.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A project life cycle consists of multiple product life cycles.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A product life cycle is composed of one or more project life cycles.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A product life cycle is composed of one or more project life cycles.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business analysis only focuses on individual projects, not the entire product life cycle.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Business analysis only focuses on individual projects, not the entire product life cycle.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Once a project is completed, the product life cycle ends.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Once a project is completed, the product life cycle ends.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9D-1\\\">During the product life cycle, a needs assessment helps align and justify the investment in a new project. Once the project is completed, a product evaluation is carried out within the product life cycle to assess whether a new project is necessary to further develop the product. Business analysis covers the entire product life cycle, including the various projects that contribute to the product's advancement.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B During the product life cycle, a needs assessment helps align and justify the investment in a new project. Once the project is completed, a product evaluation is carried out within the product life cycle to assess whether a new project is necessary to further develop the product. Business analysis covers the entire product life cycle, including the various projects that contribute to the product's advancement.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":66,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">What should the project manager do during the bidder conference? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What should the project manager do during the bidder conference? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Award the contrac<span><\\/span>t<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Award the contrac t\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Clarify any doubts<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Clarify any doubts\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Share the bid document with participants<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Share the bid document with participants\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Shortlist prospective sellers<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Shortlist prospective sellers\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Explain the bid terms and conditions<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Explain the bid terms and conditions\"}],\"key\":[\"B\",\"E\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B &amp; E<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Bidder conference, aka contractor conference or vendor conference, is arranged to ensure that sellers have a common understanding of the project procurement requirements (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 70). During the conference, the project manager and the stakeholders will discuss their procurement needs and answer any questions the sellers might have.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A &amp; D:<\\/span> In a bidder conference, the project manager does not shortlist prospective sellers or award the contract.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The bid document has to be shared with participants before the bidder conference.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B & E Bidder conference, aka contractor conference or vendor conference, is arranged to ensure that sellers have a common understanding of the project procurement requirements (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 70). During the conference, the project manager and the stakeholders will discuss their procurement needs and answer any questions the sellers might have. Options A & D: In a bidder conference, the project manager does not shortlist prospective sellers or award the contract. Option C: The bid document has to be shared with participants before the bidder conference.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":67,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">After 8 years of experience in the same position, a project manager gets promoted to a Portfolio manager role. A portfolio is:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"After 8 years of experience in the same position, a project manager gets promoted to a Portfolio manager role. A portfolio is:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A number of projects, programs, or operations that are all managed as a collection with the aim to achieve the organization’s strategic goals.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A number of projects, programs, or operations that are all managed as a collection with the aim to achieve the organization’s strategic goals.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Analyzing IT requirements and ensuring regulatory requirements are followed.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Analyzing IT requirements and ensuring regulatory requirements are followed.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Following methods, processes, and tools to ensure that projects are managed as designed.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Following methods, processes, and tools to ensure that projects are managed as designed.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Creates a common vision and helps senior management to see the potential strategic implications of corporate decisions.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Creates a common vision and helps senior management to see the potential strategic implications of corporate decisions.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A portfolio is a grouping of projects and programs. A portfolio’s purpose is to establish centralized management and oversight for a number of projects and/or programs. It also helps establish standardized governance across the organization. By creating and managing a portfolio, you’re ensuring that the organization is choosing the right projects that align with its values, strategies, and goals (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 244).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A portfolio is a grouping of projects and programs. A portfolio’s purpose is to establish centralized management and oversight for a number of projects and/or programs. It also helps establish standardized governance across the organization. By creating and managing a portfolio, you’re ensuring that the organization is choosing the right projects that align with its values, strategies, and goals (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 244).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":68,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A project manager canceled a lessons learned review meeting due to time constraints. What could be the potential consequences of this decision?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager canceled a lessons learned review meeting due to time constraints. What could be the potential consequences of this decision?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Issues faced through the project could reoccur due to the missed opportunity to identify preventive actions<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Issues faced through the project could reoccur due to the missed opportunity to identify preventive actions\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Project management will get more difficult<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project management will get more difficult\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Project cost will be greater<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project cost will be greater\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​The project may not be accepted by the Project Management Office (PMO)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The project may not be accepted by the Project Management Office (PMO)\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The knowledge acquired from the process of carrying out a project is referred to as \\\"lessons learned.\\\" This covers both the positive and negative aspects. The aim is to replicate good practices and avoid repeating errors. By failing to examine or go over past lessons learned, the project manager risks making the same errors as in previous projects. Therefore, the earlier the lessons are identified and <span><\\/span>embedded into a project, the more value they will provide. So ideally, a project manager should conduct reviews on an ongoing basis to allow for continuous improvement. Such a review will capture in-depth inputs from the project team, sponsors, stakeholders, etc. Capturing and going over lessons learned on a regular basis helps keep the project on track. In the long term, it will also help organizations continuously develop and enhance the way they conduct projects.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The knowledge acquired from the process of carrying out a project is referred to as \\\"lessons learned.\\\" This covers both the positive and negative aspects. The aim is to replicate good practices and avoid repeating errors. By failing to examine or go over past lessons learned, the project manager risks making the same errors as in previous projects. Therefore, the earlier the lessons are identified and embedded into a project, the more value they will provide. So ideally, a project manager should conduct reviews on an ongoing basis to allow for continuous improvement. Such a review will capture in-depth inputs from the project team, sponsors, stakeholders, etc. Capturing and going over lessons learned on a regular basis helps keep the project on track. In the long term, it will also help organizations continuously develop and enhance the way they conduct projects.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":69,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">The critical path method is a schedule network analysis technique. Which of the following statements is true regarding the critical path?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The critical path method is a schedule network analysis technique. Which of the following statements is true regarding the critical path?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>All of the tasks on the critical path should be critical themselves.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. All of the tasks on the critical path should be critical themselves.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>If a task in the critical path is delayed, it will result in delaying the whole project completion date.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. If a task in the critical path is delayed, it will result in delaying the whole project completion date.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A change request does not have any impact on the critical path.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A change request does not have any impact on the critical path.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The critical path can be used in both predictive and adaptive life cycles.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The critical path can be used in both predictive and adaptive life cycles.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The critical path comprises tasks that must be completed as scheduled in order for the project to be finished on time. If a task is delayed, it may cause a delay in the project’s completion date.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Some tasks on the critical path may not be critical themselves, but they need to be accomplished on time in order for the critical task(s) to be completed. The critical path method is used in projects following a predictive life cycle where change requests could have a direct impact on the project.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The critical path comprises tasks that must be completed as scheduled in order for the project to be finished on time. If a task is delayed, it may cause a delay in the project’s completion date. Option A: Some tasks on the critical path may not be critical themselves, but they need to be accomplished on time in order for the critical task(s) to be completed. The critical path method is used in projects following a predictive life cycle where change requests could have a direct impact on the project.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":70,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Who should the business analyst consult to understand the outcome of a certain process and how it meets the organization’s objectives?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Who should the business analyst consult to understand the outcome of a certain process and how it meets the organization’s objectives?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Process owner<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Process owner\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Process manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Process manager\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Product manager\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product owner<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Product owner\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Project manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Project manager\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The process owner makes sure that the process meets the target laid down by the organization and is responsible for the overall performance and effectiveness of the process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The process manager oversees the day-to-day operations of the process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The product manager is responsible for the overall strategy and vision of the product.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The product owner representing the customer, is responsible for defining and prioritizing the product backlog.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option E:<\\/span> The project manager is responsible for planning, executing, monitoring, controlling, and closing the project.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The process owner makes sure that the process meets the target laid down by the organization and is responsible for the overall performance and effectiveness of the process. Option B: The process manager oversees the day-to-day operations of the process. Option C: The product manager is responsible for the overall strategy and vision of the product. Option D: The product owner representing the customer, is responsible for defining and prioritizing the product backlog. Option E: The project manager is responsible for planning, executing, monitoring, controlling, and closing the project.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":71,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">During the execution of a construction project, the supplier informed the project manager that delivering the new order of steel bars may have a 3-day delay. What should the project manager do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During the execution of a construction project, the supplier informed the project manager that delivering the new order of steel bars may have a 3-day delay. What should the project manager do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Negotiate the delay with the vendor to get it reduced<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Negotiate the delay with the vendor to get it reduced\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Look for another vendor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Look for another vendor\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Evaluate the impact of the delay<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Evaluate the impact of the delay\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Update the project schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Update the project schedule\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager should evaluate the impact of the delay before making any decision. A delayed activity doesn’t necessarily result in the whole project delay. For instance, if the activity is not on the critical path and it has a lag of more than three days, then the delay won’t probably have any impact on the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> There is no need to negotiate the delay or look for a new vendor to get the order delivered on time.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The project manager should evaluate the impact of the delay before making any decision. A delayed activity doesn’t necessarily result in the whole project delay. For instance, if the activity is not on the critical path and it has a lag of more than three days, then the delay won’t probably have any impact on the project. Option A: There is no need to negotiate the delay or look for a new vendor to get the order delivered on time.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":72,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">During project execution, the project team had an issue with an unreliable vendor. Since the incident had a high impact on the project scope, the project manager decided to terminate the vendor’s contract and never deal with them again in the future. Where should the project manager record this issue?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During project execution, the project team had an issue with an unreliable vendor. Since the incident had a high impact on the project scope, the project manager decided to terminate the vendor’s contract and never deal with them again in the future. Where should the project manager record this issue?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lessons learned register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Lessons learned register\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Change log<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Change log\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risk register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Risk register\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Issue log<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Issue log\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The Issue Log is a project document where all information concerning faced issues is recorded and monitored (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 336).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Even though the described scenario involves lessons learned (never to deal with the unreliable vendor in the future), the question only inquires about where to record the issue<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The Issue Log is a project document where all information concerning faced issues is recorded and monitored (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 336). Option A: Even though the described scenario involves lessons learned (never to deal with the unreliable vendor in the future), the question only inquires about where to record the issue .\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":73,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">For a construction project, concrete is poured after the completion of rebar and formwork. Now, workers must wait 14 days before removing the formwork, as the concrete must be strong enough for this operation. The 14-day period is an example of:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"For a construction project, concrete is poured after the completion of rebar and formwork. Now, workers must wait 14 days before removing the formwork, as the concrete must be strong enough for this operation. The 14-day period is an example of:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A Lead<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A Lead\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A Lag<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A Lag\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Crashing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Crashing\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Fast-tracking<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Fast-tracking\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Lag Time is when a delay is purposely made between activities.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Lead time, on the other hand, is the time saved by starting an activity before its predecessor is completed.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options C &amp; D:<\\/span> Crashing and fast-tracking are two schedule compression techniques.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Lag Time is when a delay is purposely made between activities. Option A: Lead time, on the other hand, is the time saved by starting an activity before its predecessor is completed. Options C & D: Crashing and fast-tracking are two schedule compression techniques.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":74,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A new business analyst is getting hired for a new project, which competencies should the business analyst possess? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A new business analyst is getting hired for a new project, which competencies should the business analyst possess? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Analytical skills<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Analytical skills\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Expert judgment<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Expert judgment\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Personal skills<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Personal skills\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Management skills<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Management skills\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Technical skills<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Technical skills\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"B\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A, B, C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The business analyst competencies as defined in the (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, pages 53 &amp; 54) are Analytical skills, Expert judgment, Communication skills, Personal skills, Leadership skills, and Tool knowledge.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span>  Management skills are more required for project managers.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option E:<\\/span> The project team may be required to have technical skills.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, B, C The business analyst competencies as defined in the (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, pages 53 & 54) are Analytical skills, Expert judgment, Communication skills, Personal skills, Leadership skills, and Tool knowledge. Option D: Management skills are more required for project managers. Option E: The project team may be required to have technical skills.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":75,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">During which of the following meetings should the Agile project team demonstrate a potentially shippable product increment to the project stakeholders?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During which of the following meetings should the Agile project team demonstrate a potentially shippable product increment to the project stakeholders?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Review meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Review meeting\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Standup meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Standup meeting\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Retrospective meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Retrospective meeting\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Deliverables meetin<span><\\/span>g<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Deliverables meetin g\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">At the end of each iteration, the project manager and the project team should demonstrate a potentially shippable product increment to the concerned stakeholders along with the Product Owner to get their feedback. This occurs during an Iteration Review Meeting. The product owner and stakeholders use this meeting to evaluate the product and release backlog priorities (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 180).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A At the end of each iteration, the project manager and the project team should demonstrate a potentially shippable product increment to the concerned stakeholders along with the Product Owner to get their feedback. This occurs during an Iteration Review Meeting. The product owner and stakeholders use this meeting to evaluate the product and release backlog priorities (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 180).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":76,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">When the cost of quality of the project they’re leading reached a certain level, the project manager was invited to a meeting with their line manager to explain the project situation. During the meeting, the project manager was asked about the project’s cost of non-conformance. Which of the following falls under the cost of non-conformance? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"When the cost of quality of the project they’re leading reached a certain level, the project manager was invited to a meeting with their line manager to explain the project situation. During the meeting, the project manager was asked about the project’s cost of non-conformance. Which of the following falls under the cost of non-conformance? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Rework<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Rework\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scrap<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Scrap\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Warranty work<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Warranty work\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Destructive testing loss<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Destructive testing loss\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"B\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A, B, C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Destructive testing loss is an example of the cost of conformance, the rest fall under the cost of non-conformance. Cost of Non-Conformance includes the expenses arising due to non-conformance to quality requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Cost of Non-Conformance can be divided into two categories:<\\/p><ol class=\\\"class_s38-3\\\"><li><p>Internal Failure Costs are incurred when defects are detected internally (i.e. not yet presented to the customers) which include defect repair and rework. <\\/p><\\/li><li><p>External Failure Costs are incurred when defects are discovered after the deliverables have been shipped to customers (this is the worst type of quality cost) These include warranty work, liabilities, and loss of business goodwill. <\\/p><\\/li><\\/ol><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Reference: PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 89.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, B, C Destructive testing loss is an example of the cost of conformance, the rest fall under the cost of non-conformance. Cost of Non-Conformance includes the expenses arising due to non-conformance to quality requirements. Cost of Non-Conformance can be divided into two categories: Internal Failure Costs are incurred when defects are detected internally (i.e. not yet presented to the customers) which include defect repair and rework. External Failure Costs are incurred when defects are discovered after the deliverables have been shipped to customers (this is the worst type of quality cost) These include warranty work, liabilities, and loss of business goodwill. Reference: PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 89.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":77,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A new team member asks about what project management involves. The project manager answers: “Project Management is ________________________”<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A new team member asks about what project management involves. The project manager answers: “Project Management is ________________________”\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>An undertaken temporary endeavor to create a unique service, product, or result<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. An undertaken temporary endeavor to create a unique service, product, or result\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The application of a set of knowledge, skills, tools, and techniques to project activities to meet the project requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The application of a set of knowledge, skills, tools, and techniques to project activities to meet the project requirements\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The collection of programs that have been grouped to achieve strategic business goals<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The collection of programs that have been grouped to achieve strategic business goals\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>An organizational structure that aims to standardize project-related governance processes<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. An organizational structure that aims to standardize project-related governance processes\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Project management involves applying a set of processes, skills, knowledge, experience, and methods, to attain a number of predefined project objectives and requirements according to predetermined acceptance criteria (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 17).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Project management involves applying a set of processes, skills, knowledge, experience, and methods, to attain a number of predefined project objectives and requirements according to predetermined acceptance criteria (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 17).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":78,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">What added value do prototypes provide? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What added value do prototypes provide? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Allow for early feedback on the requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Allow for early feedback on the requirements\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Reduce project cost<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Reduce project cost\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Allow the project to be completed faster<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Allow the project to be completed faster\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Help to address ambiguities<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Help to address ambiguities\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Prototyping is a technique used to collect early feedback on the requirements for further refinement and clarification, along with clarifying ambiguities (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 246).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options B &amp; C:<\\/span> The development of a prototype can either increase the project cost and duration or reduce them depending on its results.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, D Prototyping is a technique used to collect early feedback on the requirements for further refinement and clarification, along with clarifying ambiguities (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 246). Options B & C: The development of a prototype can either increase the project cost and duration or reduce them depending on its results.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":79,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which is the most simple and time-efficient decision-making technique?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which is the most simple and time-efficient decision-making technique?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Alternative analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Alternative analysis\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Negotiation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Negotiation\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Escalation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Escalation\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Voting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Voting\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Voting is used to reach a consensus decision by selecting the option that gets more votes from the team members. This technique is simple, intuitive, and both time and cost-efficient.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Voting is used to reach a consensus decision by selecting the option that gets more votes from the team members. This technique is simple, intuitive, and both time and cost-efficient.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":80,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">During the last three daily standup meetings with the team, the project manager notices that a new team member is struggling with one of their assigned tasks as they seem to be making no progress towards completing it. What should the project manager do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During the last three daily standup meetings with the team, the project manager notices that a new team member is struggling with one of their assigned tasks as they seem to be making no progress towards completing it. What should the project manager do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ask an experienced team member to take over the task.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Ask an experienced team member to take over the task.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Check whether other team members can help their new colleague with the task after the standup meeting.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Check whether other team members can help their new colleague with the task after the standup meeting.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Express their disappointment to the new team member and encourage them to make more effort<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Express their disappointment to the new team member and encourage them to make more effort .\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ask the new team member to check the team ground rules.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Ask the new team member to check the team ground rules.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Asking another team member to help mentor the new member and guide them through getting their task completed and overcoming the challenging aspects of their assignment is the right course of action. Since the member is new and might lack certain skills or experience dealing with certain types of tasks, they will get the chance to learn and overcome any impediments by collaborating with more experienced team members.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Assigning someone else to get the task done will only have a bad impact on their self-esteem and motivation and make them miss out on a learning opportunity.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Similarly, expressing their disappointment at the new member’s performance will do more harm than actually resolving the issue.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Checking the team ground rules is irrelevant to this situation.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Asking another team member to help mentor the new member and guide them through getting their task completed and overcoming the challenging aspects of their assignment is the right course of action. Since the member is new and might lack certain skills or experience dealing with certain types of tasks, they will get the chance to learn and overcome any impediments by collaborating with more experienced team members. Option A: Assigning someone else to get the task done will only have a bad impact on their self-esteem and motivation and make them miss out on a learning opportunity. Option C: Similarly, expressing their disappointment at the new member’s performance will do more harm than actually resolving the issue. Option D: Checking the team ground rules is irrelevant to this situation.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":81,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">After baselining the scope and during project execution, a key stakeholder, who is a member of the Change Control Board (CCB), requested a new service. Taking into consideration that the project manager is convinced that this new service can add value to the project, what should they do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"After baselining the scope and during project execution, a key stakeholder, who is a member of the Change Control Board (CCB), requested a new service. Taking into consideration that the project manager is convinced that this new service can add value to the project, what should they do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Implement the change request since the key stakeholder is a member of the CCB.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Implement the change request since the key stakeholder is a member of the CCB.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Implement the change request since it will add value to the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Implement the change request since it will add value to the project.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Submit a change request according to the change control system.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Submit a change request according to the change control system.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Record the change request in the change log.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Record the change request in the change log.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Regardless of the fact that the change was requested by a member of the CCB, the project manager should submit a change request according to the procedures defined in the change control system. This system describes how modifications to project deliverables should be undertaken (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 332).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The project manager should not implement the change without getting the CCB’s formal approval.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Being convinced of the change’s value or having the consent of one member of the CCB is not sufficient to move forward with the implementation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The change request has not been submitted yet to the CCB, so it should not be recorded in the change log. After submitting it, the change log should be updated to track the status of the change.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Regardless of the fact that the change was requested by a member of the CCB, the project manager should submit a change request according to the procedures defined in the change control system. This system describes how modifications to project deliverables should be undertaken (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 332). Option A: The project manager should not implement the change without getting the CCB’s formal approval. Option B: Being convinced of the change’s value or having the consent of one member of the CCB is not sufficient to move forward with the implementation. Option D: The change request has not been submitted yet to the CCB, so it should not be recorded in the change log. After submitting it, the change log should be updated to track the status of the change.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":82,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">During the risk identification process, attrition of resources was identified as a major risk. As a response, the project manager decided to opt for financial incentives to motivate their team members. What type of risk response are they following?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During the risk identification process, attrition of resources was identified as a major risk. As a response, the project manager decided to opt for financial incentives to motivate their team members. What type of risk response are they following?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Acceptance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Acceptance\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Mitigation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Mitigation\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Transference<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Transference\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Avoidance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Avoidance\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager is mitigating the risk of resource attrition. This type of risk response aims to diminish the probability and/or impact of a threat (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 123).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The project manager is mitigating the risk of resource attrition. This type of risk response aims to diminish the probability and/or impact of a threat (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 123).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":83,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project task is 90% complete. It cannot, however, be finished until another task is completed. What type of dependency is this? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project task is 90% complete. It cannot, however, be finished until another task is completed. What type of dependency is this? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Finish-to-start (FS)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Finish-to-start (FS)\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Finish-to-finish (FF)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Finish-to-finish (FF)\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Mandatory dependency<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Mandatory dependency\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Discretionary dependency<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Discretionary dependency\"}],\"key\":[\"B\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B, C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">This is an example of finish-to-finish mandatory dependency. Two tasks may in fact run concurrently in the case of a finish-to-finish dependency. However, the second task can be entirely completed only after the first task is 100% done. Mandatory dependencies are those that are legally or contractually required or inherent in the nature of the work (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 60).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B, C This is an example of finish-to-finish mandatory dependency. Two tasks may in fact run concurrently in the case of a finish-to-finish dependency. However, the second task can be entirely completed only after the first task is 100% done. Mandatory dependencies are those that are legally or contractually required or inherent in the nature of the work (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 60).\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":84,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A new business analyst is hired for a large healthcare project. While going through the documents, the business analyst finds it difficult to understand the project’s goal and requirements. What should the business analyst do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A new business analyst is hired for a large healthcare project. While going through the documents, the business analyst finds it difficult to understand the project’s goal and requirements. What should the business analyst do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Ignore the understanding of the project’s goal and requirements and start planning.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Ignore the understanding of the project’s goal and requirements and start planning.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Ask the project team to help analyze the project requirements.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Ask the project team to help analyze the project requirements.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Ask the stakeholders for clarification.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Ask the stakeholders for clarification.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Stop the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Stop the project.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The Business Analyst should seek clarification from the stakeholders before making further decisions.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Planning without a clear understanding of the goals and requirements can lead to misalignment and potentially result in project failure.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> While the project team can explain the requirements, stakeholders are the primary source of requirements elicitation.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The Business Analyst should seek clarification from the stakeholders before making further decisions. Option A: Planning without a clear understanding of the goals and requirements can lead to misalignment and potentially result in project failure. Option B: While the project team can explain the requirements, stakeholders are the primary source of requirements elicitation.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":85,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is assigned to an accounting software development project. In its beta version, some users reported that the software freezes one to three times a day. Since the project manager needs more information to fix the problem, they asked the users to fill in a _______________ whenever the issue occurs to include information about how the freezing happens and how long it lasts.<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is assigned to an accounting software development project. In its beta version, some users reported that the software freezes one to three times a day. Since the project manager needs more information to fix the problem, they asked the users to fill in a _______________ whenever the issue occurs to include information about how the freezing happens and how long it lasts.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Check shee<span><\\/span>t<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Check shee t\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cheat sheet<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Cheat sheet\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Checklist<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Checklist\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Survey<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Survey\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Check sheets, aka tally sheets, are used to gather facts in order to facilitate the collection of more data concerning a potential quality issue (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 175).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A checklist is used to verify whether a set of required steps has been performed or not.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Check sheets, aka tally sheets, are used to gather facts in order to facilitate the collection of more data concerning a potential quality issue (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 175). Option C: A checklist is used to verify whether a set of required steps has been performed or not.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":86,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Moving the organization from the current state to the future state, and integrating a new solution into the organization’s operations is known as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Moving the organization from the current state to the future state, and integrating a new solution into the organization’s operations is known as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Assessing business analysis performance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Assessing business analysis performance\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business analysis planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Business analysis planning\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Assessing current state<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Assessing current state\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Transiting to future state<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Transiting to future state\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">To transition the organization from its current state to a future state and effectively integrate the new solution into operations, a readiness assessment and a transition plan must be established. These are the outcomes of the \\\"Prepare for Transition to Future State\\\" process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The process of examining the current environment under analysis to understand important factors that are internal or external to the organization, which may be the cause or reason for a problem or opportunity.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D To transition the organization from its current state to a future state and effectively integrate the new solution into operations, a readiness assessment and a transition plan must be established. These are the outcomes of the \\\"Prepare for Transition to Future State\\\" process. Option C: The process of examining the current environment under analysis to understand important factors that are internal or external to the organization, which may be the cause or reason for a problem or opportunity.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":87,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In a weak matrix organization, employees work across multiple projects and with various departments within the company to increase employee interaction and promote teamwork spirit. In the event that additional employees are needed, who is in charge of the hiring process under this matrix?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In a weak matrix organization, employees work across multiple projects and with various departments within the company to increase employee interaction and promote teamwork spirit. In the event that additional employees are needed, who is in charge of the hiring process under this matrix?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project manager​<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project manager\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The sponsor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The sponsor\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project team\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The functional manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The functional manager\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The functional manager is the one in charge of managing resources under a weak matrix. This matrix form has a huge resemblance to a traditional workplace hierarchy. A functional manager is a project’s main decision-maker as they supervise all of its aspects. Although the project manager also serves as a point of authority, they primarily report back to the functional manager.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The functional manager is the one in charge of managing resources under a weak matrix. This matrix form has a huge resemblance to a traditional workplace hierarchy. A functional manager is a project’s main decision-maker as they supervise all of its aspects. Although the project manager also serves as a point of authority, they primarily report back to the functional manager.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":88,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">In which development approach are requirements often communicated through less formal internal communications and can take the form of a prototype?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In which development approach are requirements often communicated through less formal internal communications and can take the form of a prototype?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Predictive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Predictive\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Incremental<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Incremental\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adaptive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Adaptive\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Waterfall<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Waterfall\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In Agile methodologies, an adaptive approach focuses on informal communication, iterative feedback, and the use of prototypes to continuously explore and refine requirements throughout the development process, allowing for early feedback and adjustments.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A &amp; D:<\\/span>  In predictive development approaches, aka Waterfall, requirements are typically well-defined and documented upfront. Communication is more formal and structured.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span>  Incremental development involves delivering parts of the solution in small, manageable increments. Prototyping is used less frequently than Agile as a communication tool to get feedback.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C In Agile methodologies, an adaptive approach focuses on informal communication, iterative feedback, and the use of prototypes to continuously explore and refine requirements throughout the development process, allowing for early feedback and adjustments. Options A & D: In predictive development approaches, aka Waterfall, requirements are typically well-defined and documented upfront. Communication is more formal and structured. Option B: Incremental development involves delivering parts of the solution in small, manageable increments. Prototyping is used less frequently than Agile as a communication tool to get feedback.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":89,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A senior project manager joins an ongoing project following the resignation of its former project manager. What should the new project manager do first?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A senior project manager joins an ongoing project following the resignation of its former project manager. What should the new project manager do first?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Review the project budget to determine if more funding is required.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Review the project budget to determine if more funding is required.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Go through the issue log to check the previous and current difficulties the project is facing.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Go through the issue log to check the previous and current difficulties the project is facing.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Examine the project charter to understand the project goals and deliverables.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Examine the project charter to understand the project goals and deliverables.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Add a new activity to the project schedule concerning knowledge transfer.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Add a new activity to the project schedule concerning knowledge transfer.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In order to effectively lead the project, the project manager should be fully aware of the project's purpose, priorities, and deliverables. After examining the goals and deliverables included in the project charter, the project manager should create a transition plan to help the project team cope with the unexpected change, check the project logs and reports, reassess what has been accomplished so far, and maintain the team’s commitment to the project goals and priorities.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C In order to effectively lead the project, the project manager should be fully aware of the project's purpose, priorities, and deliverables. After examining the goals and deliverables included in the project charter, the project manager should create a transition plan to help the project team cope with the unexpected change, check the project logs and reports, reassess what has been accomplished so far, and maintain the team’s commitment to the project goals and priorities.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":90,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is leading a project within a functional organization. Halfway through the project implementation, a team member left the organization. What should the project manager do first?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a project within a functional organization. Halfway through the project implementation, a team member left the organization. What should the project manager do first?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Collaborate with the functional manager to get a replacement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Collaborate with the functional manager to get a replacement\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Update the project’s resource breakdown structur<span><\\/span>e<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Update the project’s resource breakdown structur e\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Reassign their workload to the project team member<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Reassign their workload to the project team member\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Evaluate the impact of the team member’s departure on the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Evaluate the impact of the team member’s departure on the project\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">First, the project manager should understand the impact of the team member's departure on the project. It might have a big impact, therefore the leaving member needs to be promptly replaced with an experienced member. However, their departure might have a limited impact and the project can proceed without their contribution.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A &amp; C:<\\/span> Based on the evaluation findings, a decision should be taken on whether to get a replacement or reassign the workload.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The project’s resource breakdown structure should be updated later on to reflect the new changes.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D First, the project manager should understand the impact of the team member's departure on the project. It might have a big impact, therefore the leaving member needs to be promptly replaced with an experienced member. However, their departure might have a limited impact and the project can proceed without their contribution. Options A & C: Based on the evaluation findings, a decision should be taken on whether to get a replacement or reassign the workload. Option B: The project’s resource breakdown structure should be updated later on to reflect the new changes.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":91,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the following is not typically associated with business analysis?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is not typically associated with business analysis?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Determine problems and identify business needs<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Determine problems and identify business needs\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identify and recommend viable solutions<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Identify and recommend viable solutions\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Define project scope and achieve project objectives<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Define project scope and achieve project objectives\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identify and manage stakeholders<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Identify and manage stakeholders\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Ensure that the project meets the intended value<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Ensure that the project meets the intended value\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Defining the project scope and objectives is primarily the responsibility of the project manager. While the business analyst can contribute to this process, it is not the main focus of their role.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Defining the project scope and objectives is primarily the responsibility of the project manager. While the business analyst can contribute to this process, it is not the main focus of their role.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":92,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project is highly valued by the organization and is perceived as a top priority. The project manager needs to acquire resources from another project. How should the project manager allocate the team?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project is highly valued by the organization and is perceived as a top priority. The project manager needs to acquire resources from another project. How should the project manager allocate the team?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Proceed with multitasking<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Proceed with multitasking\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensure full compliance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Ensure full compliance\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Let the team members finish their project first<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Let the team members finish their project first\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ignore the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Ignore the project\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9D-1\\\">The project manager should fully allocate the team to the top-priority project, ensuring that all resources and attention are directed towards its successful completion.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The project manager should fully allocate the team to the top-priority project, ensuring that all resources and attention are directed towards its successful completion.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":93,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is leading a new virtual reality game development project. The project is scheduled to last 10 months with a budget of $100,000. One month into the project, the team completed 10% of the total work. What is the project’s current Schedule Performance Index (SPI)?​<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a new virtual reality game development project. The project is scheduled to last 10 months with a budget of $100,000. One month into the project, the team completed 10% of the total work. What is the project’s current Schedule Performance Index (SPI)?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>0.1​<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. 0.1\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>1<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. 1\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>1.1<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. 1.1\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​10<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. 10\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The schedule performance index (SPI) is a measure of the conformance of actual progress (earned value) to the planned progress: SPI = EV / PV (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 249). A value of 1.0 indicates that the project performance is on target. EV = 10% x $100,000 = $10,000, PV = (1 Month / 10 Months) x $100, 000 = $10,000 then SPI = EV / PV = 1<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A CPI or SPI that is less than 1.0 indicates poorer-than-planned project performance.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options C &amp; D:<\\/span> When CPI or SPI is greater than 1.0, it indicates better-than-planned project performance.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The schedule performance index (SPI) is a measure of the conformance of actual progress (earned value) to the planned progress: SPI = EV / PV (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 249). A value of 1.0 indicates that the project performance is on target. EV = 10% x $100,000 = $10,000, PV = (1 Month / 10 Months) x $100, 000 = $10,000 then SPI = EV / PV = 1 . Option A: A CPI or SPI that is less than 1.0 indicates poorer-than-planned project performance. Options C & D: When CPI or SPI is greater than 1.0, it indicates better-than-planned project performance.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":94,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In agile, what is the planning poker technique used for?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In agile, what is the planning poker technique used for?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Estimating how much effort is needed to complete tasks<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Estimating how much effort is needed to complete tasks\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Estimating how much work is left in the sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Estimating how much work is left in the sprint\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Testing the project and identifying blockers<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Testing the project and identifying blockers\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Measuring the sprint velocity<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Measuring the sprint velocity\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Planning poker is a card-based technique that is mostly used for estimating project activities. It is a consensus-based estimating technique (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 178). It can be used with story points, ideal days, or any other estimation unit. The estimation is done using poker cards. Team members discuss the feature, asking the product owner any questions they might have. Then, privately, each team member picks out one card that presents their estimate. All cards should be then revealed at once. If all team members select the same value, it’s set as the final estimate. Otherwise, a discussion of the different opinions and estimates will take place again before re-estimating the feature or task again.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Planning poker is a card-based technique that is mostly used for estimating project activities. It is a consensus-based estimating technique (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 178). It can be used with story points, ideal days, or any other estimation unit. The estimation is done using poker cards. Team members discuss the feature, asking the product owner any questions they might have. Then, privately, each team member picks out one card that presents their estimate. All cards should be then revealed at once. If all team members select the same value, it’s set as the final estimate. Otherwise, a discussion of the different opinions and estimates will take place again before re-estimating the feature or task again.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":95,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is leading the construction project of a luxury residency. Before proceeding with the site excavation process, a government clearance must be issued. What kind of dependency does this describe?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading the construction project of a luxury residency. Before proceeding with the site excavation process, a government clearance must be issued. What kind of dependency does this describe?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Soft logic​<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Soft logic\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Preferential logic<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Preferential logic\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>External dependency<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. External dependency\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Discretionary dependenc<span><\\/span>y<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Discretionary dependenc y\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">External dependency is the relationship between project activities and external activities that are not related to the project. Even though it’s beyond the project team’s control, such a dependency should be reflected in the project schedule.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Discretionary dependencies, also referred to as soft logic, preferred logic, or preferential logic, are not mandatory (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 60).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C External dependency is the relationship between project activities and external activities that are not related to the project. Even though it’s beyond the project team’s control, such a dependency should be reflected in the project schedule. Option D: Discretionary dependencies, also referred to as soft logic, preferred logic, or preferential logic, are not mandatory (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 60).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":96,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">During a meeting with 15 team members, the product owner was discussing and collecting ideas about the product requirements. However, since there were a lot of suggested ideas, participants decided to vote. After voting, the product owner finds that a particular idea received 9 votes, so they go with that option. What type of decision-making does this depict?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During a meeting with 15 team members, the product owner was discussing and collecting ideas about the product requirements. However, since there were a lot of suggested ideas, participants decided to vote. After voting, the product owner finds that a particular idea received 9 votes, so they go with that option. What type of decision-making does this depict?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Unanimity<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Unanimity\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Majority<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Majority\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Plurality<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Plurality\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Dictatorship<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Dictatorship\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Voting is a technique for collective decision-making which can be used to generate and prioritize project requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A, C, D:<\\/span> Unanimity, plurality, and majority are examples of voting techniques. A majority decision requires being supported by more than 50% of the group members.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Voting is a technique for collective decision-making which can be used to generate and prioritize project requirements. Options A, C, D: Unanimity, plurality, and majority are examples of voting techniques. A majority decision requires being supported by more than 50% of the group members.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":97,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A senior software engineer has recently been assigned to manage a project using the Agile approach. To ensure that they successfully deliver the project, the project manager should first:​<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A senior software engineer has recently been assigned to manage a project using the Agile approach. To ensure that they successfully deliver the project, the project manager should first:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identify all risks​<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Identify all risks\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Determine all of the sprints’ activities<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Determine all of the sprints’ activities\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Define the project success criteria<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Define the project success criteria\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Define quality metrics<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Define quality metrics\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">To ensure the successful delivery of the project, the project manager should first define success criteria with the sponsor. Agreeing upon the project’s success criteria will reduce the possibilities of its failure and reinforce its success odds. When determining the project success criteria, you should avoid using unclear and general terms and focus on being precise and clear. It’s recommended to be specific by saying, for instance: “the product should be completed by November 30th” instead of saying “the product should be completed as soon as possible”.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C To ensure the successful delivery of the project, the project manager should first define success criteria with the sponsor. Agreeing upon the project’s success criteria will reduce the possibilities of its failure and reinforce its success odds. When determining the project success criteria, you should avoid using unclear and general terms and focus on being precise and clear. It’s recommended to be specific by saying, for instance: “the product should be completed by November 30th” instead of saying “the product should be completed as soon as possible”.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":98,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is assigned to a project that follows an adaptive approach. After gathering all requirements, the project manager previewed 3 to 5 releases to achieve the project goal. They intend to define the details of each release progressively when they get more insight and feedback from key stakeholders. What should the project manager do, taking into consideration that the project has a fixed budget that cannot be exceeded?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is assigned to a project that follows an adaptive approach. After gathering all requirements, the project manager previewed 3 to 5 releases to achieve the project goal. They intend to define the details of each release progressively when they get more insight and feedback from key stakeholders. What should the project manager do, taking into consideration that the project has a fixed budget that cannot be exceeded?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Since the budget is fixed, the project manager should adopt a predictive approach for the project instead of an adaptive approach.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Since the budget is fixed, the project manager should adopt a predictive approach for the project instead of an adaptive approach.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Since chances of scope creep are high, the project manager should ensure that a Change Control Board (CCB) is established before the start of the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Since chances of scope creep are high, the project manager should ensure that a Change Control Board (CCB) is established before the start of the project.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Before the start of the project, the project manager should set a fixed number of releases and develop a detailed budget for each of them.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Before the start of the project, the project manager should set a fixed number of releases and develop a detailed budget for each of them.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project manager should work with stakeholders to prioritize work for each release until running out of budget.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The project manager should work with stakeholders to prioritize work for each release until running out of budget.\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">With an adaptive approach, the project’s cost and schedule are fixed, while the scope can be adjusted to stay within the cost constraint. Consequently, the project manager needs to prioritize the most important features when planning each release until they exhaust the whole budget<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A, B, C:<\\/span> All other options imply using the predictive approach, which won’t work for this project since its scope is unpredictable.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D With an adaptive approach, the project’s cost and schedule are fixed, while the scope can be adjusted to stay within the cost constraint. Consequently, the project manager needs to prioritize the most important features when planning each release until they exhaust the whole budget . Options A, B, C: All other options imply using the predictive approach, which won’t work for this project since its scope is unpredictable.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":99,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager depends on time-boxing to help team members avoid wasting time on shallow work and stay focused on the main deliverables. Which of the following statements best describes time-boxing?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager depends on time-boxing to help team members avoid wasting time on shallow work and stay focused on the main deliverables. Which of the following statements best describes time-boxing?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Duration of intense activity within a specific release<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Duration of intense activity within a specific release\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A time frame for executing specific activities<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A time frame for executing specific activities\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Tight planning to reduce the time required for an activity completion<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Tight planning to reduce the time required for an activity completion\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Setting a deadline for product delivery<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Setting a deadline for product delivery\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A timebox is a fixed period of time in which work has to be completed. The timebox duration could be a few hours, days, or weeks depending on the work complexity or size (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 181).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A timebox is a fixed period of time in which work has to be completed. The timebox duration could be a few hours, days, or weeks depending on the work complexity or size (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 181).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":100,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the following options falls under the project manager’s responsibilities in Agile?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following options falls under the project manager’s responsibilities in Agile?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Providing the overall strategic direction<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Providing the overall strategic direction\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Controlling the project budget<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Controlling the project budget\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Defining user stories and prioritizing the backlog<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Defining user stories and prioritizing the backlog\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensuring that the team delivers the project according to the defined requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Ensuring that the team delivers the project according to the defined requirements\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In Agile, a project manager (also known as scrum master, project team lead, or team coach) is responsible for removing impediments and ensuring that the cross-functional team performs and delivers the product as initially defined by the product owner (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 73 &amp; Agile Practice Guide, pages 40-41)<span>.<\\/span><\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D In Agile, a project manager (also known as scrum master, project team lead, or team coach) is responsible for removing impediments and ensuring that the cross-functional team performs and delivers the product as initially defined by the product owner (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 73 & Agile Practice Guide, pages 40-41) .\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":101,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is wrapping up a one-year project. Which of the following activities should be prioritized?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is wrapping up a one-year project. Which of the following activities should be prioritized?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Updating the change log<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Updating the change log\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Releasing the project resources<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Releasing the project resources\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Completing the knowledge transfer activities<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Completing the knowledge transfer activities\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Celebrating the project’s completion<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Celebrating the project’s completion\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Because projects are temporary endeavors, most of the acquired knowledge is lost once the project is completed. The project manager should be attentive to knowledge documentation and transfer to allow the organization to gain and retain the knowledge and experience obtained through running projects (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 78).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A, B, D:<\\/span> Once this activity is completed, a celebration could take place and resources can be released. On the other hand, the change log should be updated to monitor the change requests’ status.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Because projects are temporary endeavors, most of the acquired knowledge is lost once the project is completed. The project manager should be attentive to knowledge documentation and transfer to allow the organization to gain and retain the knowledge and experience obtained through running projects (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 78). Options A, B, D: Once this activity is completed, a celebration could take place and resources can be released. On the other hand, the change log should be updated to monitor the change requests’ status.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":102,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">During the last sprint, two team members took a leave. A key stakeholder wants to know how many sprints are required to complete the project. How should the project manager calculate velocity?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During the last sprint, two team members took a leave. A key stakeholder wants to know how many sprints are required to complete the project. How should the project manager calculate velocity?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use the average velocity of the last five sprints.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Use the average velocity of the last five sprints.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Use the velocity of the next sprint.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Use the velocity of the next sprint.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Increase the last velocity by 20% to compensate for the team members’ leave.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Increase the last velocity by 20% to compensate for the team members’ leave.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Use the velocity of the last sprint.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Use the velocity of the last sprint.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager should use the average velocity of the last five sprints as it gives an accurate response about the team’s capacity.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The stakeholder may need the information immediately, and cannot wait a few weeks until finishing the next sprint.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Velocity should not be altered. Besides, there is no guarantee that the contribution of the two team members is 20%.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Since two team members took leaves during the last sprint, its velocity will most probably be low and misleading.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The project manager should use the average velocity of the last five sprints as it gives an accurate response about the team’s capacity. Option B: The stakeholder may need the information immediately, and cannot wait a few weeks until finishing the next sprint. Option C: Velocity should not be altered. Besides, there is no guarantee that the contribution of the two team members is 20%. Option D: Since two team members took leaves during the last sprint, its velocity will most probably be low and misleading.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":103,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In an adaptive development approach, which tool or technique focuses on identifying and analyzing features that can deliver immediate value?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In an adaptive development approach, which tool or technique focuses on identifying and analyzing features that can deliver immediate value?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Feature injection<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Feature injection\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Story map<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Story map\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Earned value management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Earned value management\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Value stream mapping<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Value stream mapping\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Feature injection is a framework and set of principles designed to enhance and accelerate the development and analysis of product requirements. This approach is particularly favored by teams employing adaptive development methods. Its core concept is to direct discussions and analysis towards features that offer the potential for immediate value (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, pages 88 &amp; 89)<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Story map is a visual model of all the features and functionality, created to give the team a global view of what they are building.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Earned value management is used to determine the cost and schedule performance of a predictive project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options D:<\\/span> Value stream mapping is a data gathering technique used to document, analyze, and improve the flow of information or materials (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, Page 177).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Feature injection is a framework and set of principles designed to enhance and accelerate the development and analysis of product requirements. This approach is particularly favored by teams employing adaptive development methods. Its core concept is to direct discussions and analysis towards features that offer the potential for immediate value (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, pages 88 & 89) . Option B: Story map is a visual model of all the features and functionality, created to give the team a global view of what they are building. Option C: Earned value management is used to determine the cost and schedule performance of a predictive project. Options D: Value stream mapping is a data gathering technique used to document, analyze, and improve the flow of information or materials (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, Page 177).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":104,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">What is the difference between a corrective and a preventive action? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the difference between a corrective and a preventive action?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Corrective actions address what will occur in the future, while preventive actions address what already occurred in the past. <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Corrective actions address what will occur in the future, while preventive actions address what already occurred in the past.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Corrective actions address what already occurred in the past, while preventive actions address what will occur in the future. <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Corrective actions address what already occurred in the past, while preventive actions address what will occur in the future.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Corrective actions are part of the executing process group whereas preventive actions are part of the controlling and monitoring process group. <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Corrective actions are part of the executing process group whereas preventive actions are part of the controlling and monitoring process group.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Preventive actions are part of the executing process group whereas corrective actions are part of the controlling and monitoring process group. <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Preventive actions are part of the executing process group whereas corrective actions are part of the controlling and monitoring process group.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-1\\\"><span>Correct Answer = B<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-1\\\">Corrective actions are reactive as they’re performed to fix issues that have occurred to bring the project back into alignment with the baselines. Preventive actions, on the other hand, are proactive as they’re taken to ensure that the project doesn't deviate from the plan. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-2\\\"><span>Options C &amp; D:<\\/span> Both corrective and preventive actions can be part of the executing process group as well as the monitoring process group. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Corrective actions are reactive as they’re performed to fix issues that have occurred to bring the project back into alignment with the baselines. Preventive actions, on the other hand, are proactive as they’re taken to ensure that the project doesn't deviate from the plan. Options C & D: Both corrective and preventive actions can be part of the executing process group as well as the monitoring process group.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":105,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Knowledge is sometimes depicted as an iceberg since it involves two categories<span><\\/span>:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Knowledge is sometimes depicted as an iceberg since it involves two categories :\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Explicit and tacit<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Explicit and tacit\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Known and unknown<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Known and unknown\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Direct and indirect<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Direct and indirect\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Deep and superficial<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Deep and superficial\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Knowledge can be either explicit or tacit knowledge. Explicit knowledge can be expressed and captured using pictures, words, and numbers. Tacit knowledge, such as experiences and beliefs, is more difficult to express or capture (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, pages 77-78).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Knowledge can be either explicit or tacit knowledge. Explicit knowledge can be expressed and captured using pictures, words, and numbers. Tacit knowledge, such as experiences and beliefs, is more difficult to express or capture (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, pages 77-78).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":106,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A Product Owner is developing a new product and is considering the tools that will be implemented. What is the primary purpose of using product visioning techniques in this context?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A Product Owner is developing a new product and is considering the tools that will be implemented. What is the primary purpose of using product visioning techniques in this context?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Detailed project schedule establishment<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Detailed project schedule establishment\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product roadmap development<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Product roadmap development\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project team roles and responsibilities identification<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project team roles and responsibilities identification\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risk management plan creation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Risk management plan creation\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Product visioning is a tool and technique for “facilitating product roadmap development” process. It’s used to set the high-level direction for a product or a product release (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 95).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Product visioning is a tool and technique for “facilitating product roadmap development” process. It’s used to set the high-level direction for a product or a product release (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 95).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":107,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In order to ensure that the project is performed in accordance with the organization’s requirements, the project manager carries out a tailoring process. Under this context, Tailoring is:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In order to ensure that the project is performed in accordance with the organization’s requirements, the project manager carries out a tailoring process. Under this context, Tailoring is:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The knowledge and practices which are applicable to most projects in most cases.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The knowledge and practices which are applicable to most projects in most cases.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The application of a set of knowledge, skills, tools, and techniques to the project activities in order to meet its requirements.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The application of a set of knowledge, skills, tools, and techniques to the project activities in order to meet its requirements.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The selection of the appropriate processes, inputs, tools, techniques, and life cycle phases for managing a project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The selection of the appropriate processes, inputs, tools, techniques, and life cycle phases for managing a project.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The application of knowledge, skills, tools, and techniques needed for meeting a program’s requirements.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The application of knowledge, skills, tools, and techniques needed for meeting a program’s requirements.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Tailoring involves the selection of the appropriate processes, related inputs and outputs, techniques, and life cycle phases in order to manage a project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 6).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Program management is the application of knowledge, skills, tools, and techniques to meet the program requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Project management is the application of a set of knowledge, skills, tools, and techniques to project activities to meet the project requirements.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Tailoring involves the selection of the appropriate processes, related inputs and outputs, techniques, and life cycle phases in order to manage a project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 6). Option B: Program management is the application of knowledge, skills, tools, and techniques to meet the program requirements. Option D: Project management is the application of a set of knowledge, skills, tools, and techniques to project activities to meet the project requirements.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":108,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">As the roadmap is elaborated, the scope of each release may include features, functions, epics, and user stories. This decomposition process is similar to which project management tool?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"As the roadmap is elaborated, the scope of each release may include features, functions, epics, and user stories. This decomposition process is similar to which project management tool?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product Backlog<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Product Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Gantt Chart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Gantt Chart\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Kanban Board<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Kanban Board\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) is a project management tool that breaks down a project into smaller, more manageable segments, often referred to as work packages. It helps in organizing and defining the total scope of the project by creating a hierarchical decomposition of the work to be executed<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The Product Backlog is primarily a prioritized list of features, user stories, and tasks for a product. It focuses on what needs to be done and their priority but does not provide a structured breakdown of work into smaller, manageable segments like the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) does.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) is a project management tool that breaks down a project into smaller, more manageable segments, often referred to as work packages. It helps in organizing and defining the total scope of the project by creating a hierarchical decomposition of the work to be executed . Option A: The Product Backlog is primarily a prioritized list of features, user stories, and tasks for a product. It focuses on what needs to be done and their priority but does not provide a structured breakdown of work into smaller, manageable segments like the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) does.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":109,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">3 months into project execution, the sponsor gets into a financial crisis and asks the project manager to immediately end the project. What should the project manager do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"3 months into project execution, the sponsor gets into a financial crisis and asks the project manager to immediately end the project. What should the project manager do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Try to persuade the client to complete the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Try to persuade the client to complete the project\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Talk to their management about the situation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Talk to their management about the situation\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Start the close procurement process<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Start the close procurement process\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Start the close project process<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Start the close project process\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">When the project is closed or terminated for any reason, the project manager should start the close process. Procurement closure is part of the \\\"Close project\\\" process. The situation in the question requires project termination, so the Correct Answer implies executing the process that addresses the situation, i.e. the Close Project process. Plus, there is no indication in the question that the project has procurements.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D When the project is closed or terminated for any reason, the project manager should start the close process. Procurement closure is part of the \\\"Close project\\\" process. The situation in the question requires project termination, so the Correct Answer implies executing the process that addresses the situation, i.e. the Close Project process. Plus, there is no indication in the question that the project has procurements.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":110,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is leading a team with distributed members across different countries. Apart from cultural barriers, the team seems disconnected, leading to multiple rework cases. What could the project manager do to improve communication within the team?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a team with distributed members across different countries. Apart from cultural barriers, the team seems disconnected, leading to multiple rework cases. What could the project manager do to improve communication within the team?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Collaborate with senior management to co-locate the team.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Collaborate with senior management to co-locate the team.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Request from the team to only use emails for communication to avoid any misunderstanding or misinterpretation.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Request from the team to only use emails for communication to avoid any misunderstanding or misinterpretation.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Hold short daily meetings with all team members to sync on what everyone is doing.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Hold short daily meetings with all team members to sync on what everyone is doing.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Offer team members training about overcoming cultural barriers.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Offer team members training about overcoming cultural barriers.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Short daily meetings are referred to as daily standup meetings which represent a framework for sharing what each member has accomplished, what they will be doing next, and what blockers they’re facing. This type of meeting helps build a connection between team members, improves communication, and as a result reduces rework. Co-location can resolve this issue too. However, team members are dispersed in different countries, making it difficult to assemble them in one location.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Written, asynchronous communication such as emails does not promote bonding or building connections in comparison to verbal synchronous channels such as virtual meetings<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Offering team members training about cultural differences could only help them overcome cultural barriers, but it can’t help them sync their work to avoid rework.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Short daily meetings are referred to as daily standup meetings which represent a framework for sharing what each member has accomplished, what they will be doing next, and what blockers they’re facing. This type of meeting helps build a connection between team members, improves communication, and as a result reduces rework. Co-location can resolve this issue too. However, team members are dispersed in different countries, making it difficult to assemble them in one location. Option B: Written, asynchronous communication such as emails does not promote bonding or building connections in comparison to verbal synchronous channels such as virtual meetings Option D: Offering team members training about cultural differences could only help them overcome cultural barriers, but it can’t help them sync their work to avoid rework.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":111,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">An organization asked the project manager to send a report on the cost of quality. The report stated that the total cost was $30,000, detailed as follows:<\\/p><table class=\\\"class_s1Z2\\\"><tbody><tr><td>Item<\\/td><td>Training<\\/td><td>Rework<\\/td><td>Inspection<\\/td><td>Scrap<\\/td><td>Warranty charges<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Cost<\\/td><td>$10,000<\\/td><td>$10,000<\\/td><td>$5,000<\\/td><td>$3,000<\\/td><td>$2,000<\\/td><\\/tr><\\/tbody><\\/table><p class=\\\"class_s1GS-0\\\">According to the above table, how much is the appraisal cost of the project?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An organization asked the project manager to send a report on the cost of quality. The report stated that the total cost was $30,000, detailed as follows: Item Training Rework Inspection Scrap Warranty charges Cost $10,000 $10,000 $5,000 $3,000 $2,000 According to the above table, how much is the appraisal cost of the project?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>$2,000<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. $2,000\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>$3,000<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. $3,000\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>$5,000<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. $5,000\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>$10,000<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. $10,000\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Appraisal costs, also known as inspection costs, are part of the Cost of Conformance as they represent the costs of identifying defective products before they are delivered to clients. This comprises testing, inspecting, auditing, evaluating, and measuring the deliverables, products, or services the project is producing. Appraisal costs are set up to implement a series of activities to determine work results’ degree of conformance to quality requirements. This means that the project appraisal cost involves inspection costs which are $5,000. Training falls under prevention activities. Rework and scrap costs, on the other hand, are part of the Internal Failure Costs, whereas Warranty charges fall under External Failure Costs.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Appraisal costs, also known as inspection costs, are part of the Cost of Conformance as they represent the costs of identifying defective products before they are delivered to clients. This comprises testing, inspecting, auditing, evaluating, and measuring the deliverables, products, or services the project is producing. Appraisal costs are set up to implement a series of activities to determine work results’ degree of conformance to quality requirements. This means that the project appraisal cost involves inspection costs which are $5,000. Training falls under prevention activities. Rework and scrap costs, on the other hand, are part of the Internal Failure Costs, whereas Warranty charges fall under External Failure Costs.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":112,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">All of the following are either Agile or Lean frameworks except:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"All of the following are either Agile or Lean frameworks except:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scrumban<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Scrumban\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>eXtreme Programming<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. eXtreme Programming\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Waterfall<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Waterfall\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Crystal Methods<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Crystal Methods\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Waterfall is a predictive methodology that was deemed too rigid to handle the changing requirements brought on by new technology or a demanding client. Even though there are numerous Agile and Lean frameworks, the Agile Practice Guide only addresses Scrum, Scrum of scrums, SAFe, Kanban Method, Scrumban, eXtreme Programming (XP), Crystal Methods, Dynamic Systems Development Method (DSDM), Feature-Driven Development (FDD), and Agile Unified Process<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Waterfall is a predictive methodology that was deemed too rigid to handle the changing requirements brought on by new technology or a demanding client. Even though there are numerous Agile and Lean frameworks, the Agile Practice Guide only addresses Scrum, Scrum of scrums, SAFe, Kanban Method, Scrumban, eXtreme Programming (XP), Crystal Methods, Dynamic Systems Development Method (DSDM), Feature-Driven Development (FDD), and Agile Unified Process .\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":113,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is leading a construction project. Work on light spots is pending since ceiling tiles are still being installed, which may cause some delays within the project. What should the project manager refer to in order to check the electricity team’s availability in the next two weeks to resolve this dependency?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a construction project. Work on light spots is pending since ceiling tiles are still being installed, which may cause some delays within the project. What should the project manager refer to in order to check the electricity team’s availability in the next two weeks to resolve this dependency?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource Calendars<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Resource Calendars\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM​)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM)\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>RACI​ Matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. RACI Matrix\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Organigram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Organigram\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A resource calendar is a calendar for planning, managing, and monitoring resources, including both employees and equipment. It gives project managers an overview of how resources are being utilized, which resources are available, and when.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM) describes the involvement of different parties and their roles in completing tasks or deliverables in a project. It's used to clarify roles and responsibilities within a team, project, or process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> RACI is an acronym for Responsible Accountable Consult and Inform and it’s used to assign roles and responsibilities for each task in a given process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> An organigram, also called an organizational chart, organogram, or organizational breakdown structure (OBS), is a diagram that depicts the organization’s structure and the relationships and ranks of its different positions.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A resource calendar is a calendar for planning, managing, and monitoring resources, including both employees and equipment. It gives project managers an overview of how resources are being utilized, which resources are available, and when. Option B: The Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM) describes the involvement of different parties and their roles in completing tasks or deliverables in a project. It's used to clarify roles and responsibilities within a team, project, or process. Option C: RACI is an acronym for Responsible Accountable Consult and Inform and it’s used to assign roles and responsibilities for each task in a given process. Option D: An organigram, also called an organizational chart, organogram, or organizational breakdown structure (OBS), is a diagram that depicts the organization’s structure and the relationships and ranks of its different positions.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":114,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">While traditional project management follows predefined phases and sticks to the predetermined scope, Agile project management approaches<span><\\/span>:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"While traditional project management follows predefined phases and sticks to the predetermined scope, Agile project management approaches :\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Encapsulate analysis, design, implementation, and testing within an iteration.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Encapsulate analysis, design, implementation, and testing within an iteration.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Involve documenting, estimating, and sequencing each planned activity in detail.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Involve documenting, estimating, and sequencing each planned activity in detail.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use Gantt charts along with well-defined activities, responsibilities, and time frames.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Use Gantt charts along with well-defined activities, responsibilities, and time frames.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Map the iteration backlog into a Work Breakdown Structure (WBS).<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Map the iteration backlog into a Work Breakdown Structure (WBS).\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The iterative method is the heart of the Agile development process. Each iteration generates a piece of the product until the final product is fully completed and delivered.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A typical iteration process flow involves:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">-<span>         <\\/span>Analysis: to define the iteration requirements based on the product backlog, sprint backlog, and feedback from customers and stakeholders.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">-<span>         <\\/span>Development: includes design and implementation based on the defined requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">-<span>         <\\/span>Testing: involves Quality Assurance testing.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">-<span>         <\\/span>Delivery: integrating the working iteration into production,<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">-<span>         <\\/span>Feedback: receiving customer and stakeholder feedback to define the requirements of the next iteration.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The iterative method is the heart of the Agile development process. Each iteration generates a piece of the product until the final product is fully completed and delivered. A typical iteration process flow involves: - Analysis: to define the iteration requirements based on the product backlog, sprint backlog, and feedback from customers and stakeholders. - Development: includes design and implementation based on the defined requirements. - Testing: involves Quality Assurance testing. - Delivery: integrating the working iteration into production, - Feedback: receiving customer and stakeholder feedback to define the requirements of the next iteration.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":115,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Grade and quality are two of the most commonly used terms in project management on a daily basis. Which of these statements is correct when talking about a performed service or a developed product?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Grade and quality are two of the most commonly used terms in project management on a daily basis. Which of these statements is correct when talking about a performed service or a developed product?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Low quality is acceptable, but a low grade is not<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Low quality is acceptable, but a low grade is not\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A low grade is acceptable, but a low quality is not<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A low grade is acceptable, but a low quality is not\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Low grade and low quality are both unacceptable<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Low grade and low quality are both unacceptable\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Quality and grade are the same<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Quality and grade are the same\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Grade refers to a category or rank given to entities having the same functional use but different technical characteristics. A product can be of a high-grade (high-end) or low-grade (low-end). A low-grade product is perfectly acceptable, as long as it fulfills requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A &amp; C:<\\/span> A low-quality product is always a problem and is never acceptable. Every produced item must have high quality regardless of its grade; no one wants a low-quality product. Example: You buy a basic model (low-grade) cell phone with no advanced features, but it works well. Thus, we’re talking about a high-quality product. Although it is low-grade, it keeps you satisfied (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 241).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Grade refers to a category or rank given to entities having the same functional use but different technical characteristics. A product can be of a high-grade (high-end) or low-grade (low-end). A low-grade product is perfectly acceptable, as long as it fulfills requirements. Options A & C: A low-quality product is always a problem and is never acceptable. Every produced item must have high quality regardless of its grade; no one wants a low-quality product. Example: You buy a basic model (low-grade) cell phone with no advanced features, but it works well. Thus, we’re talking about a high-quality product. Although it is low-grade, it keeps you satisfied (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 241).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":116,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which type of information radiator shows the amount of remaining work in a sprint?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which type of information radiator shows the amount of remaining work in a sprint?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Velocity chart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Velocity chart\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Burndown chart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Burndown chart\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cumulative flow diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Cumulative flow diagram\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Burnup chart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Burnup chart\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A burndown chart visually represents the remaining story points or the reduction in risk exposure over time<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Velocity chart tracks the rate at which the deliverables are produced, validated, and accepted within a predefined interval.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A chart indicating features completed over time, features in other states of development, and those in the backlog.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A burnup chart can track the actual work completed in relation to the total work expected to be done.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A burndown chart visually represents the remaining story points or the reduction in risk exposure over time . Option A: Velocity chart tracks the rate at which the deliverables are produced, validated, and accepted within a predefined interval. Option C: A chart indicating features completed over time, features in other states of development, and those in the backlog. Option D: A burnup chart can track the actual work completed in relation to the total work expected to be done.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":117,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">After a brainstorming session, what technique is used to organize and categorize the elaborated ideas into groups?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"After a brainstorming session, what technique is used to organize and categorize the elaborated ideas into groups?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p>SWOT analysis <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"SWOT analysis\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-1\\\"><p><span>Mind mapping<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Mind mapping\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-1\\\"><p><span>Affinity diagram<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Affinity diagram\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-1\\\"><p><span>Fishbone diagram<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Fishbone diagram\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">An Affinity Diagram is a tool used to organize and categorize ideas or information generated during a brainstorming session into related groups or themes. It helps to bring order to a large volume of data by grouping similar ideas together, making it easier to see patterns and relationships. This technique is especially useful when dealing with complex issues or when the brainstorming session produces a lot of ideas that need to be sorted and prioritized (Business analysis for practitioners, page 105).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> SWOT Analysis (Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, and Threats) is a strategic planning tool used to identify and evaluate the internal and external factors that can affect a project or business. It’s not used for organizing or categorizing ideas from a brainstorming session, but rather for analyzing specific aspects of a situation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Mind Mapping is a technique used to visually organize information around a central concept, often involving a hierarchical or branching structure. While it can be used to explore ideas, it is not specifically designed for categorizing and grouping them into related themes, which is what an Affinity Diagram does.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A Fishbone Diagram, also known as a Cause-and-Effect Diagram or Ishikawa Diagram, is used to identify the root causes of a problem. It categorizes potential causes of problems in a structured manner but is not primarily intended for organizing ideas generated in a brainstorming session into groups.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C An Affinity Diagram is a tool used to organize and categorize ideas or information generated during a brainstorming session into related groups or themes. It helps to bring order to a large volume of data by grouping similar ideas together, making it easier to see patterns and relationships. This technique is especially useful when dealing with complex issues or when the brainstorming session produces a lot of ideas that need to be sorted and prioritized (Business analysis for practitioners, page 105). Option A: SWOT Analysis (Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, and Threats) is a strategic planning tool used to identify and evaluate the internal and external factors that can affect a project or business. It’s not used for organizing or categorizing ideas from a brainstorming session, but rather for analyzing specific aspects of a situation. Option B: Mind Mapping is a technique used to visually organize information around a central concept, often involving a hierarchical or branching structure. While it can be used to explore ideas, it is not specifically designed for categorizing and grouping them into related themes, which is what an Affinity Diagram does. Option D: A Fishbone Diagram, also known as a Cause-and-Effect Diagram or Ishikawa Diagram, is used to identify the root causes of a problem. It categorizes potential causes of problems in a structured manner but is not primarily intended for organizing ideas generated in a brainstorming session into groups.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":118,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Halfway through the iteration, the project manager realizes that some user stories are unexpectedly delayed. Along with identifying any potential impediments, the project manager works on helping their team ______________ Work In Progress (WIP).<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Halfway through the iteration, the project manager realizes that some user stories are unexpectedly delayed. Along with identifying any potential impediments, the project manager works on helping their team ______________ Work In Progress (WIP).\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Increase<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Increase\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Limit<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Limit\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Compress<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Compress\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Skip<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Skip\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">To improve productivity and efficiency, an agile team needs to limit Work In Progress (WIP). Limiting work in progress is a technique to troubleshoot unexpected or unforeseen delays (Agile Practice Guide, page 59).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B To improve productivity and efficiency, an agile team needs to limit Work In Progress (WIP). Limiting work in progress is a technique to troubleshoot unexpected or unforeseen delays (Agile Practice Guide, page 59).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":119,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A Scrum Master attends or facilitates the different Scrum events including the Sprint, Sprint planning, Daily standup, Sprint review, and Sprint retrospective. Which of the following options describes the sprint retrospective meeting?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A Scrum Master attends or facilitates the different Scrum events including the Sprint, Sprint planning, Daily standup, Sprint review, and Sprint retrospective. Which of the following options describes the sprint retrospective meeting?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A meeting for refining product backlog items<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A meeting for refining product backlog items .\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A meeting for discussing the negative and positive aspects of a sprint as well as any possible improvements.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A meeting for discussing the negative and positive aspects of a sprint as well as any possible improvements.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A meeting for defining and evaluating the work of the next sprint.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A meeting for defining and evaluating the work of the next sprint.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A meeting held at the end of the project’s last sprint.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. A meeting held at the end of the project’s last sprint.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">During the sprint retrospective meeting, all the good and bad aspects of the sprint are discussed. The retrospective meeting is considered a meeting for improvements, as it is mainly held to find the proper ways and means of identifying potential pitfalls and past errors, and to seek out new ways to avoid those mistakes. This meeting isn't held at the end of the project’s last sprint; it recurrently takes place after the Sprint Review and before the following Sprint Planning.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A backlog refinement meeting is used to refine product backlog items<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The sprint planning meeting is used to define and evaluate the work of the next sprint.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B During the sprint retrospective meeting, all the good and bad aspects of the sprint are discussed. The retrospective meeting is considered a meeting for improvements, as it is mainly held to find the proper ways and means of identifying potential pitfalls and past errors, and to seek out new ways to avoid those mistakes. This meeting isn't held at the end of the project’s last sprint; it recurrently takes place after the Sprint Review and before the following Sprint Planning. Option A: A backlog refinement meeting is used to refine product backlog items . Option C: The sprint planning meeting is used to define and evaluate the work of the next sprint.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":120,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">An organization is making a progressive transition from the predictive to the adaptive approach. What can the project manager do to prepare their team for the transition? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An organization is making a progressive transition from the predictive to the adaptive approach. What can the project manager do to prepare their team for the transition? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Provide training for the team on agile values and practices.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Provide training for the team on agile values and practices.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Apply the “learning-by-doing” philosophy by immediately switching to agile approaches.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Apply the “learning-by-doing” philosophy by immediately switching to agile approaches.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Plan a gradual transition by introducing a few iterative or incremental techniques to their current project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Plan a gradual transition by introducing a few iterative or incremental techniques to their current project.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Suggest a full transition since agile practices cannot be combined with predictive ones.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Suggest a full transition since agile practices cannot be combined with predictive ones.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A, C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager should provide their team with relevant training in order to enable them to adopt the new agile practices with more confidence. They should also gradually introduce certain iterative or incremental techniques to make the transition smoother. This will improve the team learning process and accelerate delivering value to sponsors. Many teams can’t make a full immediate switch to the agile approach. It is preferable and even recommended to make a gradual transition by combining adaptive and predictive practices, which is known as a hybrid approach (Agile Practice Guide, page 30).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, C The project manager should provide their team with relevant training in order to enable them to adopt the new agile practices with more confidence. They should also gradually introduce certain iterative or incremental techniques to make the transition smoother. This will improve the team learning process and accelerate delivering value to sponsors. Many teams can’t make a full immediate switch to the agile approach. It is preferable and even recommended to make a gradual transition by combining adaptive and predictive practices, which is known as a hybrid approach (Agile Practice Guide, page 30).\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":121,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the following entities is responsible for establishing standardized project governance processes across an organization by defining project management frameworks and templates?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following entities is responsible for establishing standardized project governance processes across an organization by defining project management frameworks and templates?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project management office<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project management office\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Value delivery office<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Value delivery office\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Steering committee<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Steering committee\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Testing unit<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Testing unit\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A management structure that standardizes project governance processes and promotes the sharing of resources, methodologies, tools, and techniques (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 245).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The value delivery office focuses on ensuring that projects deliver value to the organization. It is not responsible for establishing standardized project management frameworks and templates.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A steering committee provides strategic direction and oversight for projects and programs. It sets priorities and approves significant decisions, but it does not create or define standardized project management processes or templates.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The testing unit is responsible for testing products or systems to ensure they meet quality standards. Its focus is on quality assurance rather than defining project management frameworks and templates.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A management structure that standardizes project governance processes and promotes the sharing of resources, methodologies, tools, and techniques (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 245). Option B: The value delivery office focuses on ensuring that projects deliver value to the organization. It is not responsible for establishing standardized project management frameworks and templates. Option C: A steering committee provides strategic direction and oversight for projects and programs. It sets priorities and approves significant decisions, but it does not create or define standardized project management processes or templates. Option D: The testing unit is responsible for testing products or systems to ensure they meet quality standards. Its focus is on quality assurance rather than defining project management frameworks and templates.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":122,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">What does servant leadership imply?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What does servant leadership imply?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>One individual in charge of directing and guiding the team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. One individual in charge of directing and guiding the team\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Carrying out work through iterations, with one prominent leader<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Carrying out work through iterations, with one prominent leader\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Naming a team leader, while team members serve as followers<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Naming a team leader, while team members serve as followers\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Understanding and addressing the needs of team members<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Understanding and addressing the needs of team members\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">According to the Agile Practice Guide, servant leadership implies leading your team by focusing on understanding and addressing their needs to yield the best performance possible (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 17).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D According to the Agile Practice Guide, servant leadership implies leading your team by focusing on understanding and addressing their needs to yield the best performance possible (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 17).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":123,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager created the following high-level hierarchical list of human and physical resources of a project that consists in creating a bulk SMS platform for marketing campaigns. What does this visual illustration represent?<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sFS-0\\\" id=\\\"page_81\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager created the following high-level hierarchical list of human and physical resources of a project that consists in creating a bulk SMS platform for marketing campaigns. What does this visual illustration represent?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Resource calendar<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Resource calendar\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Organization breakdown structure<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Organization breakdown structure\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Resource breakdown structure<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Resource breakdown structure\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​RACI chart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. RACI chart\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A resource breakdown structure is a hierarchical list of team and physical resources related by category and resource type that is used for project planning, management, and control (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 187). Each descending level corresponds to a more detailed description of the resource.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A resource calendar, on the other hand, is a calendar for planning, managing, and monitoring resources.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Organizational Breakdown Structure (OBS), also known as Organization Chart, is used for representing the project organization<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> RACI is an acronym for Responsible Accountable Consult and Inform and it’s used to assign the roles and responsibilities of the individuals involved in a project or a process.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A resource breakdown structure is a hierarchical list of team and physical resources related by category and resource type that is used for project planning, management, and control (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 187). Each descending level corresponds to a more detailed description of the resource. Option A: A resource calendar, on the other hand, is a calendar for planning, managing, and monitoring resources. Option B: Organizational Breakdown Structure (OBS), also known as Organization Chart, is used for representing the project organization . Option D: RACI is an acronym for Responsible Accountable Consult and Inform and it’s used to assign the roles and responsibilities of the individuals involved in a project or a process.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":124,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">An organization is conducting several projects, each with its own deadline, which requires assigning the available resources simultaneously to different projects. Concerned about potential delays in her project, a project manager consults with the functional manager to discuss the allocation of additional resources. Which is the most crucial skill for the project manager in this situation?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An organization is conducting several projects, each with its own deadline, which requires assigning the available resources simultaneously to different projects. Concerned about potential delays in her project, a project manager consults with the functional manager to discuss the allocation of additional resources. Which is the most crucial skill for the project manager in this situation?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Planning\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Negotiation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Negotiation\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Facilitation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Facilitation\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Documentation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Documentation\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Negotiation is the most important skill for project managers to have when working with extremely limited budgets and resource allocations.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Negotiation is the most important skill for project managers to have when working with extremely limited budgets and resource allocations.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":125,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the following Scrum meetings is product-centered?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following Scrum meetings is product-centered?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Daily standup<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Daily standup\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Sprint planning\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint review<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Sprint review\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint retrospective<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Sprint retrospective\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The Sprint Review is a product-centered meeting, during which the agile team demonstrates the functionalities they have completed during the sprint, seeking the Product Owner's feedback and approval (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 179).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The Sprint Review is a product-centered meeting, during which the agile team demonstrates the functionalities they have completed during the sprint, seeking the Product Owner's feedback and approval (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 179).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":126,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">After defining the project’s high-level requirements, the agile team along with the product owner begins writing down a list of the product features, including short descriptions of all the functionalities they’re going to deliver. Next, they’re going to prioritize the product backlog based on:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"After defining the project’s high-level requirements, the agile team along with the product owner begins writing down a list of the product features, including short descriptions of all the functionalities they’re going to deliver. Next, they’re going to prioritize the product backlog based on:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The value of the items<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The value of the items\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The complexity of the items<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The complexity of the items\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The size of the items<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The size of the items\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The risk associated with the items<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The risk associated with the items\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The product backlog should be prioritized and organized based on the value that each item brings to the product and project. This value depends on several factors such as the item’s complexity, criticality, and the risk associated with it. However, these factors are not the basis for determining the items’ value. Each item’s value is dictated by the Product Owner as well as the items’ sequence in the product backlog.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The product backlog should be prioritized and organized based on the value that each item brings to the product and project. This value depends on several factors such as the item’s complexity, criticality, and the risk associated with it. However, these factors are not the basis for determining the items’ value. Each item’s value is dictated by the Product Owner as well as the items’ sequence in the product backlog.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":127,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager was asked to lead a project of flight booking website development. The airline requested that the website should be able to support one thousand visitors per hour. This condition is also known as a(n): (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager was asked to lead a project of flight booking website development. The airline requested that the website should be able to support one thousand visitors per hour. This condition is also known as a(n): (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Requirement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Requirement\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Scope\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Acceptance criterion<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Acceptance criterion\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Deliverable<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Deliverable\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A, C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The condition of supporting one thousand visitors per hour is considered a requirement and an acceptance criterion for the project. A requirement is defined as “a condition or capability that is necessary to be present in a product, service, or result to satisfy a business need.” (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 82). Acceptance criteria are conditions required to be met before deliverables are accepted. This condition cannot be considered a deliverable or scope on its own.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The project scope, on the other hand, represents the overall amount of work required to achieve the project’s main objectives.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Deliverables refer to quantifiable products or services that must be delivered by the end of the project, i.e., the flight booking website.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, C The condition of supporting one thousand visitors per hour is considered a requirement and an acceptance criterion for the project. A requirement is defined as “a condition or capability that is necessary to be present in a product, service, or result to satisfy a business need.” (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 82). Acceptance criteria are conditions required to be met before deliverables are accepted. This condition cannot be considered a deliverable or scope on its own. Option B: The project scope, on the other hand, represents the overall amount of work required to achieve the project’s main objectives. Option D: Deliverables refer to quantifiable products or services that must be delivered by the end of the project, i.e., the flight booking website.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":128,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is leading an iterative project. The product owner calls for a meeting with the project team and other prominent stakeholders to review a demonstration of the produced deliverable. When should the project manager organize this meeting?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading an iterative project. The product owner calls for a meeting with the project team and other prominent stakeholders to review a demonstration of the produced deliverable. When should the project manager organize this meeting?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>At the beginning of every iteration<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. At the beginning of every iteration\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>At the end of every iteration<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. At the end of every iteration\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>At the end of the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. At the end of the project\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>At the start of the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. At the start of the project\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Iteration review meetings take place at the end of each iteration to allow the project team to obtain feedback from the product owner and concerned stakeholders on a regular basis.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Iteration review meetings take place at the end of each iteration to allow the project team to obtain feedback from the product owner and concerned stakeholders on a regular basis.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":129,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">One of the project team’s key members leaves the project for personal reasons. The project manager did not plan for such a scenario but they managed to get a replacement with the help of a staffing agency. However, they have to pay them a higher salary. This will result in extra costs which fall under the project’s:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"One of the project team’s key members leaves the project for personal reasons. The project manager did not plan for such a scenario but they managed to get a replacement with the help of a staffing agency. However, they have to pay them a higher salary. This will result in extra costs which fall under the project’s:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Contingency reserve<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Contingency reserve\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Cost\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Management reserve<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Management reserve\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Budget<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Budget\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Management reserve involves the dedicated budget or time reserve for handling unidentified risks or unknown unknowns (unknown = unidentified, unknowns = risks). This type of reserve is not a calculated budget and does not take part in the cost baseline. Therefore, anytime an unknown risk occurs, the project manager will need permission to use this reserve<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A contingency reserve is used for identified risks with predetermined risk response strategies, aka known-unknowns (known = identified, Unknowns = risks) (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 127).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Management reserve involves the dedicated budget or time reserve for handling unidentified risks or unknown unknowns (unknown = unidentified, unknowns = risks). This type of reserve is not a calculated budget and does not take part in the cost baseline. Therefore, anytime an unknown risk occurs, the project manager will need permission to use this reserve . Option A: A contingency reserve is used for identified risks with predetermined risk response strategies, aka known-unknowns (known = identified, Unknowns = risks) (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 127).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":130,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager was assigned to develop a mobile app with a team of five members. Which of the following project life cycles can be adopted by the project manager?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager was assigned to develop a mobile app with a team of five members. Which of the following project life cycles can be adopted by the project manager?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Initiation, planning, executing, monitoring and controlling, and closing.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Initiation, planning, executing, monitoring and controlling, and closing.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Wireframing, prototyping, designing, developing, testing, and deploying.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Wireframing, prototyping, designing, developing, testing, and deploying.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Development, introduction, growth, maturity, and decline.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Development, introduction, growth, maturity, and decline.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Forming, storming, norming, performing, and adjourning.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Forming, storming, norming, performing, and adjourning.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project life cycle that can be adopted for developing a mobile app project is: Wireframing, prototyping, designing, developing, testing, and deploying. A project life cycle comprises the different development phases that a project goes through from its start to its completion. Depending on different factors, a project lifecycle often includes Feasibility, Design, Build, Test, Deploy, and Close phases (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, pages 33-42).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Initiation, planning, executing, monitoring and controlling, and closing are process groups rather than project lifecycle phases.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Forming, storming, norming, performing, and adjourning are team development phases according to Tuckman’s theory.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The project life cycle that can be adopted for developing a mobile app project is: Wireframing, prototyping, designing, developing, testing, and deploying. A project life cycle comprises the different development phases that a project goes through from its start to its completion. Depending on different factors, a project lifecycle often includes Feasibility, Design, Build, Test, Deploy, and Close phases (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, pages 33-42). Option A: Initiation, planning, executing, monitoring and controlling, and closing are process groups rather than project lifecycle phases. Option D: Forming, storming, norming, performing, and adjourning are team development phases according to Tuckman’s theory.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":131,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sPA-1\\\">Place the following project budget components in the right position in the figure below: <span>Project budget<\\/span> - <span>Cost baseline<\\/span> - <span>Contingency reserve<\\/span> - <span>Management reserve<\\/span>.<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sFS-0\\\" id=\\\"page_83\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"Place the following project budget components in the right position in the figure below: Project budget - Cost baseline - Contingency reserve - Management reserve .\",\"choices\":[],\"key\":[],\"answerHtml\":\"<div class=\\\"class_s76-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\">The project total amount is composed of the management reserve and the project budget, which in turn is composed of the cost baseline and contingency reserve (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 63). Therefore, A = Management reserve, B = Project budget, C = Contingency reserve, and D = Cost baseline.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"The project total amount is composed of the management reserve and the project budget, which in turn is composed of the cost baseline and contingency reserve (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 63). Therefore, A = Management reserve, B = Project budget, C = Contingency reserve, and D = Cost baseline.\",\"type\":\"mapping\",\"special\":{\"type\":\"mapping\",\"targets\":[[\"A\",\"A\"],[\"B\",\"B\"],[\"C\",\"C\"],[\"D\",\"D\"]],\"options\":[[\"project-budget\",\"Project budget\"],[\"cost-baseline\",\"Cost baseline\"],[\"contingency\",\"Contingency reserve\"],[\"management\",\"Management reserve\"]],\"correct\":{\"A\":\"management\",\"B\":\"project-budget\",\"C\":\"contingency\",\"D\":\"cost-baseline\"}},\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":132,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In order to handle high levels of change and ensure the active participation of all interested parties, a project manager adopts a change-driven project development approach, which is also known as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In order to handle high levels of change and ensure the active participation of all interested parties, a project manager adopts a change-driven project development approach, which is also known as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adaptive approach<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Adaptive approach\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Predictive approach<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Predictive approach\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Waterfall approach<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Waterfall approach\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Hybrid approach<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Hybrid approach\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A change-driven approach is also referred to as an adaptive, Agile, flexible, or change-focused approach. This development approach is characterized by the ability to react and adapt to high levels of change as well as the constant involvement and participation of different parties<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A waterfall or predictive approach is sequential and rigid.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Hybrid is a combination of predictive and adaptive approaches.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A change-driven approach is also referred to as an adaptive, Agile, flexible, or change-focused approach. This development approach is characterized by the ability to react and adapt to high levels of change as well as the constant involvement and participation of different parties . Option C: A waterfall or predictive approach is sequential and rigid. Option D: Hybrid is a combination of predictive and adaptive approaches.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":133,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A business analyst is assessing the business needs for a certain project. Which tool or technique involves conducting a study in which it evaluates different factors that could lead to valuable recommendations?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst is assessing the business needs for a certain project. Which tool or technique involves conducting a study in which it evaluates different factors that could lead to valuable recommendations?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Feasibility analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Feasibility analysis\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>SWOT analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. SWOT analysis\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risk assessment<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Risk assessment\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost-Benefit Analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Cost-Benefit Analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Feasibility analysis involves assessing various factors to evaluate the viability of different options being considered. (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 86)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A cost-benefit analysis evaluates the financial return of implementing the solution by comparing the expected benefits against the costs. It's an effective way to assess the business value of a solution.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Feasibility analysis involves assessing various factors to evaluate the viability of different options being considered. (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 86) Option D: A cost-benefit analysis evaluates the financial return of implementing the solution by comparing the expected benefits against the costs. It's an effective way to assess the business value of a solution.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":134,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Working in a predictive environment, a project manager has decided to use a three-point estimation with a beta distribution to measure the cost of project activities.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s1GS-0\\\">Which of the following formulas should the project manager use?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Working in a predictive environment, a project manager has decided to use a three-point estimation with a beta distribution to measure the cost of project activities. Which of the following formulas should the project manager use?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>(Optimistic + Pessimistic + Most likely) ÷ 3<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. (Optimistic + Pessimistic + Most likely) ÷ 3\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>(Optimistic + Pessimistic + (2 × Most likely)) ÷ 4<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. (Optimistic + Pessimistic + (2 × Most likely)) ÷ 4\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>(Optimistic + Pessimistic + (3 × Most likely)) ÷ 5<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. (Optimistic + Pessimistic + (3 × Most likely)) ÷ 5\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>(Optimistic + Pessimistic + (4 × Most likely)) ÷ 6<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. (Optimistic + Pessimistic + (4 × Most likely)) ÷ 6\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The three-point estimation formula using a beta (weighted average) distribution is as follows: (Optimistic + Pessimistic + (4 × Most likely)) ÷ 6.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The three-point estimation formula uses a triangular distribution (simple average) as follows: (Optimistic + Pessimistic + Most likely) ÷ 3.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The three-point estimation formula using a beta (weighted average) distribution is as follows: (Optimistic + Pessimistic + (4 × Most likely)) ÷ 6. Option A: The three-point estimation formula uses a triangular distribution (simple average) as follows: (Optimistic + Pessimistic + Most likely) ÷ 3.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":135,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the following is not considered an elicitation technique?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is not considered an elicitation technique?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Brainstorming<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Brainstorming\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Document analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Document analysis\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Observation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Observation\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Interviews<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Interviews\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Use case<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Use case\"}],\"key\":[\"E\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = E<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A use case is a tool and technique used to define and elaborate requirements, not to conduct the elicitation process. All the other options are tools and techniques for conducting the elicitation process (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 164).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = E A use case is a tool and technique used to define and elaborate requirements, not to conduct the elicitation process. All the other options are tools and techniques for conducting the elicitation process (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 164).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":136,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is leading a construction project. In order to track the project's progress, the project manager sets milestones in the project schedule. What is the typical duration of a milestone?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a construction project. In order to track the project's progress, the project manager sets milestones in the project schedule. What is the typical duration of a milestone?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Half of the project duration<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Half of the project duration\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The same duration as the project life cycle<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The same duration as the project life cycle\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Zero<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Zero\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>One mont<span><\\/span>h<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. One mont h\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The duration of a milestone is zero because it denotes a significant achievement, point, or event in a project, such as the completion of a particular deliverable for instance (PMI - Process groups guide, page 213).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The duration of a milestone is zero because it denotes a significant achievement, point, or event in a project, such as the completion of a particular deliverable for instance (PMI - Process groups guide, page 213).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":137,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sFM-0\\\">In order to gather end-user feedback, a senior project manager of an Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) project discusses several ideas with the project team and then they draw the following diagram. What tool are they using?<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_s24D-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,";
